WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.260
- I learned over time

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.910
that you have to create
your own boundaries.

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.690
People aren't just gonna give them to you.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.290
- Oh, lord.
- And it's okay.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.610
Yeah, I need a whole show
about boundaries, y'all.

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.395
It ain't my forte.

00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:12.228
(Khloe laughs)

00:00:12.228 --> 00:00:14.510
- It's not so many people's fortes,

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:16.640
but you have to learn to...

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.860
It to feel not so guilty demanding them,

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:21.790
because it's sad that
you have to say a demand,

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.120
but it turns out to be,

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.240
'cause everybody wants a piece of you.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:26.740
But I think the most important person

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.240
that deserves a piece of
you would be your babies,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.060
and you have to give them that
and it's okay to demand that.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:35.450
And I think anybody will understand

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.560
when it comes to your children.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.393
- Absolutely.

00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:39.226
It's interesting though,

00:00:39.226 --> 00:00:40.330
I wish I would've learned

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.460
how to have better boundaries
though before children,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:46.380
'cause now it is a good out to be like,

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:47.690
look, this is my kids and they get,

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.720
everybody kinda understands that,

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:49.600
but before you have kids

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.670
and you're like just single,
rocking it in an industry,

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.450
and trying to make it or any industry,

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.870
it's okay to say like, I'm
tired, I need a minute.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.700
Like, but it's almost awesome
when you do have kids,

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:02.430
'cause you're like, look,
I really need a minute,

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.250
and people see like
something physically there,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.240
but I wish people...

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:08.670
I wish I had learned that
sooner when I was younger.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.060
I was not good at that.

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.100
- Yeah, and I agree.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.500
I think when I was
younger before I had kids,

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.800
I felt so guilty to...

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.980
Like I wasn't almost worthy
- Me too.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.000
of having a boundary 'cause
I didn't have a real reason.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.240
That sounds so strange,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:23.870
but that's almost how I felt,

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:26.030
like, oh, no one's gonna really care

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:27.450
about what my boundary is,

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.250
'cause I don't have a real responsibility

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.560
or something that I need to get home to.

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:32.560
But you do.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:35.440
Self-care is a good enough reason.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.560
Just because you're tired
or you need a break,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.980
that's valid enough for a boundary.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.930
And I don't know if
it's just 'cause of age

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.470
or I just was insecure or whatever,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:48.470
I just didn't feel it was okay
to use that as my boundary.

